      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — See inline comments for issues that must be addressed before merging.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** Correctly fixes the sysjump tag size check in `ap_sku_id_restore_state()` from `sizeof(prev_ap_sku_id)` (which evaluates to pointer size, 8 bytes on 64-bit host/POSIX builds) to `sizeof(ap_sku_id)` (4 bytes, `uint32_t`), matching `ap_sku_id_preserve_state()` and the `memcpy()` call on line 124.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Fits cleanly within the existing `common/system.c` sysjump state preservation and restoration pattern.\n* **Code Simplicity:** Minimal, focused 1-line fix with no unnecessary complexity.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Follows ChromiumOS EC C conventions by using `sizeof(ap_sku_id)` directly on the destination variable.\n* **Security:** Ensures `memcpy(\u0026ap_sku_id, prev_ap_sku_id, sizeof(ap_sku_id))` only executes when the stored tag payload size matches the 4-byte `ap_sku_id` buffer size across both 32-bit and 64-bit targets.\n* **Testing:** Missing unit test coverage for `ap_sku_id_restore_state()` (both happy-path sysjump preservation/restoration and negative boundary cases for missing tag, version mismatch, and size mismatch); `drivers.system` does not currently enable `CONFIG_HOSTCMD_AP_SET_SKUID` or test AP SKU ID restoration.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** XS (+1, -1 lines), single self-contained logical fix.\n* **Commit Message:** Concise and accurate summary line and body explaining both what changed and why (`sizeof(prev_ap_sku_id)` vs `sizeof(ap_sku_id)` on 64-bit targets), with `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/f9f74a07-936d-4f97-adba-425d7d5c05bf)",
